        "text": "In this module we will learn what is market psychology and how that affects market cycles. Market psychology is the idea that the movements of a market reflect or are influenced by the emotional state of its participants. It's one of the main topics of behavioral economics, an interdisciplinary field that studies the various factors that precede economic decisions. Many believe that emotions are the main driving force behind the shifts of financial markets and that the overall fluctuating investor sentiment is what creates the so called psychological market cycles. Market sentiment is the overall feeling that investors and traders have regarding the price action of an asset. The sentiment is made up of the individual views and feelings of all traders and investors within a financial market. You can also think of it as an average of the overall feeling of the market participants, but just as with any group, no single opinion is completely dominant.",
